#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:7
msgid "Manage your connected devices"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:9
msgid ""
"Openhub lists and manages the devices connected to your computer: Bluetooth, "
"USB, power, mice, keyboards, audio and displays."
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:11
msgid "See every connected device at a glance, with low batteries flagged"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:12
msgid ""
"See your computer's processor, memory, graphics, disk and system versions, "
"and copy them for a bug report"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:13
msgid ""
"Check the firmware of your laptop and devices, and whether an update is "
"available"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:14
msgid ""
"See your devices' batteries, Bluetooth connections and sound output from the "
"top bar, with the optional GNOME Shell extension"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:15
msgid "Turn Bluetooth on and off"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:16
msgid ""
"See your Bluetooth devices, whether they're connected, and their battery "
"level"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid "Scan for nearby devices and pair them"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:18
msgid "Connect, disconnect, trust, block and forget Bluetooth devices"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:19
msgid ""
"See your USB devices as they're plugged in, grouped under the hubs they're "
"connected through"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid "Check a USB device's speed, version, power draw and driver"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:21
msgid "Safely eject USB drives"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:22
msgid ""
"See your laptop's battery and the battery of every wireless device in one "
"place"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid "Check battery health, charge cycles and energy"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:24
msgid ""
"Preserve battery health by stopping charging at 80%, on laptops that support "
"it"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:25
msgid ""
"Change the DPI, scroll wheel and buttons of Logitech, Razer and other gaming "
"mice"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:26
msgid "Change the lighting and keys of VIA keyboards, stored on the keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:27
msgid ""
"Choose your audio output and input, set their volume, and see each "
"microphone's level"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:28
msgid "Shape each output's sound with a 10-band equalizer or an AutoEQ profile"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:29
msgid ""
"Arrange your displays and set their resolution, refresh rate, scale and "
"orientation, as GNOME Settings does"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:30
msgid ""
"Set the brightness of the built-in screen and of external monitors that "
"support DDC/CI"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:31
msgid ""
"Turn on Night Light, choose each display's color profile, and turn on HDR "
"where supported"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:35
msgid "CJ"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:41
msgid "The System page: every connected device, and this computer's details"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:45
msgid "Bluetooth devices, connected ones first, with their batteries"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:49
msgid ""
"Displays, with their arrangement, settings, brightness and color profile"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:53
msgid "Audio outputs and inputs, with volume, mute and microphone levels"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:57
msgid "Mice and touchpads, with their connection and battery"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:61
msgid "Keyboards, with their connection and battery"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:65
msgid ""
"The laptop's battery, the charge limit and every wireless device's battery"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:69
msgid "USB devices, grouped under the hubs they're connected through"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:93
msgid "A new look for the GNOME Shell extension's menu:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:95
msgid ""
"A header with a settings button that opens Openhub, and a Bluetooth card"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:96
msgid ""
"Batteries and Sound Output are sections that collapse and expand smoothly"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:97
msgid ""
"Each battery shows its icon, level and a bar; the current sound output has a "
"radio mark"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:98
msgid ""
"Colours follow the shell theme, including custom themes, and stay readable "
"over a blurred menu"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:104
msgid ""
"Adds an optional GNOME Shell extension, with Openhub's icon in the top bar:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:106
msgid ""
"The battery of every mouse, keyboard and headset, lowest first, with a level "
"bar in the shell theme's colours and a warning below 20%"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:107
msgid ""
"The number of connected Bluetooth devices, and a list of sound outputs to "
"switch between"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:108
msgid "Each row opens Openhub on that page; it works without Openhub running"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:109
msgid "The System page shows whether it's installed, and turns it on and off"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:110
msgid "The Power page's level bars now use the accent colour"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:116
msgid "Openhub 1.0 adds a System page, the first page Openhub opens on:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:118
msgid ""
"Connected Devices: a card for each page with what's connected there, one "
"count of every device, and a warning for low batteries"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:119
msgid ""
"About this computer: model, processor, memory, graphics, disk, firmware, "
"operating system, desktop and kernel, with Copy Details for bug reports"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:120
msgid ""
"Device Firmware: the firmware of your laptop, drives and devices from fwupd, "
"with update notes and a link to GNOME Software to install"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:121
msgid ""
"Links to the GNOME Settings pages for device name, region, date and time, "
"users and remote access"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:122
msgid "The sidebar is reordered, and every page now fits a phone-sized window"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:128
msgid "Adds a Displays page:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:130
msgid ""
"Arrange displays by dragging them, and choose Join, Mirror or a single "
"display, with an Identify button"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:131
msgid ""
"Resolution, refresh rate, variable refresh rate, scale and orientation for "
"each display, applied with GNOME's \"Keep these display settings?\" check"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:132
msgid ""
"Brightness of the built-in screen, following the brightness keys, and of "
"external monitors over DDC/CI"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:133
msgid ""
"Night Light: on and off, sunset to sunrise or set times, and the color "
"temperature"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:134
msgid ""
"Color profiles through colord: choose, import and remove, with a link to "
"GNOME Settings to calibrate"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:135
msgid "HDR on displays that support it"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:136
msgid "A details dialog for each display, read from its EDID"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:142
msgid "A new app icon, and clearer setup for the Flatpak:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:144
msgid ""
"A new icon: a ring of devices around a switch, in Catppuccin colours, with a "
"matching symbolic icon"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:145
msgid ""
"The README copies the udev rules from the installed Flatpak, so Flatpak "
"users don't need the source code"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:151
msgid "Security and reliability fixes:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:153
msgid ""
"The VIA and Razer udev rules now open only the interface Openhub uses, so a "
"keyboard's own interface can't be read by other programs"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:154
msgid ""
"A VIA keyboard sending unexpected replies, or an unusual VIA definition "
"file, can no longer crash Openhub"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:155
msgid ""
"Equalizer settings are saved only for outputs with ordinary names, so a "
"crafted output name can't change WirePlumber's configuration"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:161
msgid "Adds Mouse, Keyboard and Audio pages:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:163
msgid ""
"Logitech mice: DPI, SmartShift and scroll direction, restored automatically "
"when the mouse reconnects"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:164
msgid ""
"Razer mice: DPI and polling rate, stored on the mouse; other brands through "
"ratbagd"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:165
msgid ""
"VIA keyboards on their cable: lighting and key remapping from the keyboard's "
"VIA definition, and a shortcut to GNOME Settings' keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:166
msgid ""
"Audio outputs and inputs: default device, volume, mute, Bluetooth codec and "
"a live microphone level"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:167
msgid ""
"A built-in equalizer for each output, with presets and AutoEQ import, that "
"keeps working when Openhub is closed"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:168
msgid ""
"Batteries the kernel reports but UPower misses, such as some 2.4 GHz mice"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:174
msgid "Adds a Power page:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:176
msgid ""
"The laptop's battery level and charging state, and the battery of every "
"wireless mouse, keyboard or headset UPower knows about, updated live"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:177
msgid ""
"Battery details: health, charge cycles, energy, charge rate, voltage and "
"technology"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:178
msgid ""
"A \"Preserve Battery Health\" setting that stops charging at the laptop's "
"limit, shown only where it's supported"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:179
msgid "Low batteries shown in the warning colour"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:181
msgid ""
"On the USB page, a wireless receiver now shows the battery of the devices it "
"serves."
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:186
msgid "Adds a USB page:"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:188
msgid ""
"A live list of USB devices, grouped under the hubs they're connected "
"through, with microphones and speakers recognized"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:189
msgid ""
"Details for each device: IDs and serial number (with copy buttons), speed, "
"USB version, power draw, class and driver"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:190
msgid "Safe eject for USB drives, including encrypted ones"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:191
msgid ""
"Built-in devices such as cameras and fingerprint readers hidden unless you "
"ask for them"
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:193
msgid ""
"Bluetooth: connected devices are listed first, connecting shows progress, "
"pairing pauses scanning, and blueman's connection notifications, which can "
"freeze GNOME Shell, are turned off when blueman is running."
msgstr ""

#: data/openhub.metainfo.xml.in:198
msgid ""
"The first release, for Bluetooth: power the adapter on and off, connect and "
"disconnect paired devices, scan for and pair new ones, and trust, block or "
"forget them."
msgstr ""

